# Merge policy for append-only ledgers.
#
# `merge=union` keeps BOTH sides' lines on a conflict. It is correct ONLY for
# strictly append-only, line-oriented files where two branches add entries in
# any order and neither rewrites existing lines. Do NOT extend it to:
#   - structured files (JSON/YAML): union produces duplicate keys / invalid data.
#     e.g. scripts/guardrails_ratchet.json is an in-place counter map — a
#     concurrent bump is a 4-key hand-merge, or fix it with a max-merge driver.
#   - living docs rewritten in place (docs/alignment_state_of_record.md): a
#     concurrent /align-checkpoint is a semantic conflict a human must reconcile;
#     union would splice two different "current-best" narratives together.

# Closed-experiments ledger — append-only, matched by basename so it holds
# regardless of directory (attic/ today, archive/experiments/ if promoted).
EXPERIMENTS.md merge=union
